[{:db/id 17592186064211 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-ba9103c6-cd4f-5fe9-b177-f46928ef48cb" "question-400c3acc-5e79-52be-941c-8ede9d67d05b"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186064073 :question/problem "Calculate the value of $2+ (-6).$" :question/worked-solution "We drop the parentheses and the addition sign to give \n\n$$\n2+ (-6) = 2-6.\n$$\n\n \n\nThen, we move $6$ spaces to the left of $2$ on a number line.\n\n![](images/ed/ed6c51ffa37fa80ca17575c241738c602cb81cb2bca500fea1fb3231063763b2.png)\n\nWe end up at $-4.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n2 + (-6) = -4.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186064212 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-e1a479d0-fff3-5ce1-b03e-c90e28459585" "question-f9cc8296-f82a-5b59-ab73-a756fc3da0a9"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186064074 :question/problem "What is the value of $-1 + (- 2.5)?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we drop the parentheses and the addition sign, which gives\n\n$$\n-1 + (- 2.5) = -1 - 2.5.\n$$\n\nThen, we carry out the subtraction as usual. This gives\n\n$$\n-1 - 2.5 = -3.5.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186064213 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-4ba4fabf-8311-5600-bcfe-05b44a10e255" "question-17e6f69c-9289-5c2f-847c-503ec0fb9123"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186064076 :question/problem "Find the value of $-\\dfrac{2}{5} + \\left(- \\dfrac{3}{10}\\right).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we drop the parentheses and the addition sign, which gives\n\n$$\n-\\dfrac 2 5 + \\left(-\\dfrac{3}{10}\\right) = -\\dfrac 2 5 -\\dfrac{3}{10} .\n$$\n\nNow, we need to convert the fractions to have the same denominator. To convert $-\\dfrac{2}{5}$ to have a denominator of $10,$ we multiply the numerator and denominator by $2$ as follows:\n\n$$\n- \\dfrac{2}{5} = - \\dfrac{2 \\times 2}{5 \\times 2} = - \\dfrac{4}{10}\n$$\n\nNow, the subtraction problem is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2}{5}-\\frac{3}{10} & =-\\frac{4}{10}-\\frac{3}{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBecause the two fractions now have the same denominator, we can combine the numerators:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{4}{10}-\\frac{3}{10}=\\frac{-4-3}{10}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we work out $-4 - 3$ using our number line.\n\n![](images/dd/dd96e6f3b2a3e35d0f792cb828ef905cfb0ea86b0962b017ceaa0630e4aba144.png)\n\nWe find that $-4-3=-7.$ So, we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac {-4 - 3} {10} = \\dfrac{-7}{10} = -\\dfrac{7}{10} .\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-ba9103c6-cd4f-5fe9-b177-f46928ef48cb" :question/id #uuid "ba9103c6-cd4f-5fe9-b177-f46928ef48cb" :question/math-academy-id "q-6127" :question/problem "What is $170+(-70)?$" :question/worked-solution "We drop the parentheses and the addition sign to give \n\n$$\n170+(-70)=170-70.\n$$\n\n \n\nThen, we carry out the subtraction as usual. This gives\n \n\n$$\n170-70=100.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-17c89d3f-1f1c-5a32-b35d-3f19c82047a0"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-17c89d3f-1f1c-5a32-b35d-3f19c82047a0" :answer-field/id #uuid "17c89d3f-1f1c-5a32-b35d-3f19c82047a0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-3ac01d11-7fca-5866-9f35-fc51aef94fd5" :answer-field/choices ["answer-924f556a-1a02-506e-8aa9-357927ea6268" "answer-7ed42e4a-b79d-5685-a49e-233ca7338787" "answer-3ac01d11-7fca-5866-9f35-fc51aef94fd5" "answer-523ea15b-7817-5cc6-9723-b93a5c21253d" "answer-6c2385dd-e704-5a6f-a5a8-c37149fa46c1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-924f556a-1a02-506e-8aa9-357927ea6268" :answer/id #uuid "924f556a-1a02-506e-8aa9-357927ea6268" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-100" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7ed42e4a-b79d-5685-a49e-233ca7338787" :answer/id #uuid "7ed42e4a-b79d-5685-a49e-233ca7338787" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-240" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "a